# A FACT AS A CALL ARGUMENT CROSSES AS ITS FactExternal (RFCS.23.1).
#
# The trace prints a fact argument as its FactExternal bytes, so the two
# runtimes' encodings of one fact are compared byte for byte: the schema, the
# schema_hash over the SchemaShape (RFCS.23.3), the fields in declaration
# order (RFCS.23.4) and its asserted_at (RFCS.23.5); a FactExternal carries no
# event_id. A field either runtime spelled differently, or a hash over the
# slots in another order, is a diff line here.
#
# The fact is HOST-asserted, so both runtimes have stamped it before the pump
# that fires the call. A fact a rule emitted earlier in the same pump is
# 93_call_emitted's case.
# @spec [NCBK.6.10] [RFCS.23.4] [RFCS.23.5]
assert Reading id="k" n=3 x=2.5 ok=true
pump
